 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive tier V membership in the New York state and local\nemployees' retirement system to Daniel Miller",
    "basePrintNo": "S6166",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6166-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6166\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act granting retroactive tier V membership in the New York state and\nlocal employees' retirement system to Daniel Miller\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant Daniel Miller retroactive tier V membership in the\nNew York State and Local Employees Retirement System.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill changes Daniel Miller's effective membership date\nin the New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System from May\n21, 2012 to March 7, 2012 so that he may be placed in the Tier V retire-\nment group. He shall file with the State Comptroller a written request\nto this effect and, upon granting of such retroactive membership, Mr.\nMiller will not be granted a refund of any employee contribution made by\nhim to the system.\n\nSection 2 of the bill describes who is responsible for any past cost\nincurred in implementing the provisions of this act.\n\nSection 3 of the bill is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDaniel Miller commenced employment in the Town of Hempstead on March 7,\n2012, which should have entitled him to Tier V membership in the New\nYork State and Local Employees' Retirement System. However, due to a\nclerical error made by the Town of Hempstead, Mr.  Miller was not\nentered in the retirement system until May 21, 2012, granting him Tier\nVI membership, and he should not be penalized for the clerical error.\n\nThis bill, if enacted into law, would correct the mistake by allowing\nDaniel Miller to file for retroactive membership in the New York State\nand Local Employees' Retirement System as of March 7, 2012, the day of\nhis actual employment.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note appended to bill.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
